# SquirrElix benchmarking (agents)

When an implementation round can affect performance — codegen, SQL parsing,
Postgres infer, output write path, drift check, or generated runtime
encode/decode — follow the process in [`docs/PERFORMANCE.md`](../../docs/PERFORMANCE.md).
That file is the source of truth; do not invent absolute CI timing gates.

## Required loop

1. Run `mix bench` **before** hot-path edits when a baseline is needed.
2. Implement (and prefer `mix precommit` for correctness).
3. Re-run the **same** bench after under comparable conditions.
4. Record meaningful before→after in `docs/PERFORMANCE.md` (and `CHANGELOG.md`
   when appropriate).
5. Do **not** document noise or insignificant jitter.
6. Avoid performance regressions; call out real improvements.
7. Soft CI only — never add hard absolute µs/ms fail gates.

Skip the bench loop only for docs-only, pure test fixtures, or changes clearly
off the hot path.
